%% Nous: a road's closure lifecycle (finding (a) invariant made visual).
%% Key invariant: time + reads alone NEVER reopen a closed road. Decay is a pure
%% read-only view; closure changes ONLY on an active crossing.
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Open: add_road (faint dirt, strength 0.05)
    Open --> Open: strengthen / traverse (quality climbs dirt to highway)
    Open --> Closed: strong NEGATIVE crossing (valence <= -0.75) or one-shot trauma
    Closed --> Open: ACTIVE POSITIVE return (valence >= -0.30) reopens it

    note right of Open
        Reads apply decay as a COPY (a view).
        Stored state is never changed by a read.
    end note
    note right of Closed
        Sticky: time passing and repeated reads
        do NOT reopen it. Only an active positive
        crossing does. (Avoidance preserves trauma.)
    end note
